@startuml doorbell-delivery
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Doorbell: delivering a message into a hosted session

participant "Tracked run\n(terminal hook)" as R $AGENT
queue "Per-session inbox\n(manager state)" as I $PRIVATE
participant "Notice pump\n(session host)" as Pump $SERVICE
participant "Provider host" as H $SERVICE
participant "Hosted primary session" as S $AGENT
participant "Main loop" as M $SERVICE

== Today ==
R -> I: DeliverTerminal: one durable notice per terminal run
Pump -> I: tick, or a nudge on attach
alt running, host implements ProviderSessionNotifier, at least one client attached
  Pump -> H: DeliverSessionNotice(coalesced text)
  H -> S: bracketed paste (Claude) / app-server turn (Codex)
else no client attached
  Pump -> Pump: keep the notices queued
  note right of Pump
    replayed as one message
    on the next attach
  end note
end

== Target (requirement R4) ==
M -> I: waggle message addressed to the session\n(request, wake)
Pump -> H: deliver with or without an attached client,\naccording to the delivery policy
H -> S: next turn, or interrupt
S --> M: reports over waggle

caption Sources: docs/claude-goal-runtime.md "In-session run notices"; internal/sessionmanager/manager_notice.go; spec §2.5, §5
@enduml
